    "created_at": "2022-05-25T07:02:28Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-05-25T07:02:28Z",
    "body": "I think there's a slight difference there that @johannhof made me aware of at some point, in that restricting the referrer forces the \"attack\" to become more visible and also reduces the number of channels you have to protect (i.e., reduced to just the URL). I think that is a compelling reason for referrer restrictions in general. I suppose I don't care too strongly about this particular issue, though I would favor following the general model of HTTP headers generally being authoritative.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
